crown: Pass the microphones through Amazon's Voice pipeline

Amazon's Voice pipeline, which the HAL runs for VoIP captures, has an AGC
that turned the level down by up to 25 dB after a loud sound and kept it
there. In passthrough it leaves captures alone. Amazon's ASR pipeline, its
far-field front end for the wake word, stays on: the Kiosk Satellite
Edition sends plain mic captures through it (ro.vendor.audio.asr_capture).

diff --git a/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg b/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
index 896bd06..17c92ba 100644
--- a/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
+++ b/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
